    "body": "Re-rated P7 → P1 (M3, from the review of PR #1600, pullrequestreview-5900043149): in every 3-axis Tormach program the tool change is `G53 G0 Z0`, `G30`, `T M6`, `G43`, `S M3`, `M8`, then `G0 X Y` with **no Z lift between** (e.g. `drill_plate.nc:7-14`, `probe_guard_moves.nc:7-12`). With a low stored G30 (as the user's Hub sim had - the same cause as #1594's slam) the tool drops to G30 Z and then rapids sideways at that height: a collision the post emits silently, every program. Only 4th-axis sections re-lift. Suggested fix: `G53 G0 Z<safe>` after the `G43` line, before the first XY rapid. The kit README's 'keep G30 Z at the top' is the workaround (so P3 at the very least).",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
